# CLOSURE (qa-pr1182-r3, quality-mgr): arch-ctm's fix-aw3-r3 remediation
# (feature/aw3-health-and-log-query @ db47e09c9, module-extraction into
# router_support.rs/runtime_listener.rs/loopback_read.rs/doctor_observability.rs)
# moved both files under the RULE-003 1000-non-test-line cap. Independently
# confirmed via #[cfg(test)] mod tests boundary at db47e09c9: lib.rs boundary
# at line 924 (923 non-test lines), storage_and_nudge_router.rs boundary at
# line 979 (978 non-test lines). req-qa's qa-pr1182-r3 round additionally
# recomputed true blank/comment-stripped production-line counts (~720/~867)
# using .just/lint_common.py's classify_rust_test_scope, confirming an even
# wider margin under cap. arch-qa and rust-qa-agent independently corroborated
# the raw boundary-line counts at the current commit. Both occurrences closed.
#
# NOTE: arch-qa's qa-pr1182-r3 pass surfaced a separate, NEW RULE-003
# violation not in this finding's original scope: crates/atm-http-runtime/src/client.rs
# is at 1297 non-test lines (boundary at line 1298), confirmed by quality-mgr
# to already be at 1285 non-test lines back at the AW.3 round-1 tip 199a3bfeb
# (i.e. pre-existing, not introduced by this fix round, but touched in-diff
# this round). Filed as a new finding and routed to team-lead triage
# separately -- not folded into this record.

